<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ho Chi Minh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nguyen Ai Quoc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ho Chi Minh was a Vietnamese revolutionary who helped found the French Communist Party and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochinese-communist-party">Indochinese Communist Party</a>, and in 1941 formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution">August Revolution</a> of 1945 he proclaimed the independence of the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>. As its president he led the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> in 1954, and the struggle to reunify Vietnam, dying in 1969 before it was achieved.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh.jpg" alt="Ho Chi Minh" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ho_Chi_Minh_-_1946_Portrait_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
